{"ok":true,"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00431","versions":[{"version_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00431@rel:R25-11#4a523943","canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00431","release":"R25-11","content":"function OpenFileWriteOnly [SWS_PER_00431] Upstream: RS_PER_00001 , RS_PER_00004 , RS_PER_00010 , RS_AP_00119 , RS_AP_00120 , RS_AP_00121 , RS_AP_00127 , RS_AP_00128 , RS_AP_00129 , RS_AP_00135 , RS_AP_00139 , RS_AP_00144 , RS_AP_00159 ara::core::Result &lt; UniqueHandle &lt; WriteAccessor &gt; &gt; OpenFileWriteOnly ( ara::core::StringView fileName, OpenMode mode, ara::core::Span &lt; ara::core::Byte &gt; buffer) noexcept; Opens a file of this File Storage for writing with a user provided buffer. If not otherwise specified by the provided mode, the file is truncated (corresponding to k Truncate). The provided buffer will be used by the ReadWriteAccessor to implement block-wise writing to speed up multiple small accesses to the file. If the file does not exist, it is created. The file will be closed when the returned UniqueHandle goes out of scope. Header-Datei #include \"ara/per/file_storage.h\" class mono Scope class ara::per::FileStorage class mono Exception-Sicherheit exception safe class mono Thread-Sicherheit thread-safe class mono Parameter (in) th Parameter th Beschreibung td fileName td File name of the file. May correspond to the PersistencyFile.file Name of a configured file. td mode td Mode with which the file shall be opened. td buffer td Memory to be used for block-wise writing. Rückgabewert th Typ th Beschreibung td ara::core::Result &lt; UniqueHandle &lt; WriteAccessor &gt; &gt; td A Result containing a UniqueHandle for the file. In case of an error, it contains any of the errors defined below, or a vendor specific error. Fehler th Fehlercode th Beschreibung td PerErrc ::kIllegalWriteAccess td rollback_semantics Returned if the File Storage is configured as read-only, or if it is configured as write-only-once and the key already exists. td PerErrc ::kPhysicalStorageFailure td no_rollback_semantics Returned if access to the physical storage fails. td PerErrc ::kIntegrityCorrupted td rollback_semantics Returned if stored data cannot be read because the structural integrity is corrupted. td PerErrc ::kValidationFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if the validity of stored data cannot be ensured. td PerErrc ::kEncryptionFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if the decryption of stored data fails. td PerErrc ::kResourceBusy td rollback_semantics Returned if the file is already open, or if DeleteFile, RecoverFile, or ResetFile with the same file name is currently being executed. td PerErrc ::kOutOfStorageSpace td no_rollback_semantics Returned if the available physical storage space is insufficient for a new file. td PerErrc ::kInvalidOpenMode td rollback_semantics Returned if the passed mode contains an invalid combination of modes. td PerErrc ::kTooManyFiles td rollback_semantics Returned if the number of files would get larger than the configured maxNumberOfFiles when the file is created. td PerErrc ::kAuthenticationFailed td rollback_semantics Returned if checking the MAC of stored data fails.","meta":{"trigger_kind":"baseline_sync"},"recorded_at":"2026-09-30T16:43:34+00:00"}],"lifecycle":{"canonical_id":"AUTOSAR/AP/record/SWS_PER_00431","is_dropped":false,"first_active_release":"R25-11","last_active_release":"R25-11","dropped_in":[],"first_dropped_release":null,"absent_before":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11"],"platform_releases":["R19-11","R20-11","R21-11","R22-11","R23-11","R24-11","R25-11"],"latest_platform_release":"R25-11"},"element":{"kind":"function","name":"OpenFileWriteOnly","module":"PER","cluster":"","page":"classes/cl_ara_per_FileStorage_29266b.html","doc_type":"SWS","ai":false,"first":"R25-11","last":"R25-11","changed":[],"distinct":1,"universe":"AP"},"evidence":{"figures":[{"id":"FIG-bc38ec7d6cc22ce1","doc":"AUTOSAR_AP_SWS_VehicleUpdateAndConfigurationManageme